1. Purpose
This software, source code, scripts, workflows, documentation, and associated materials
(the "Materials") are made publicly accessible primarily for transparency, peer review,
and reproducibility assessment of the associated scientific work.

2. Permission Required for Reuse
Except for viewing, downloading, and executing the Materials solely for the purpose of
verifying or reproducing the results of the associated publication, no permission is
granted for reuse.

Prior written permission from the corresponding author or copyright holder is required
before any of the following:
- use of the Materials in a new research project;
- modification, adaptation, translation, or derivative development;
- redistribution or republication of the Materials;
- incorporation into another software package, workflow, database, or online service;
- use of the Materials to generate results intended for publication, presentation,
  grant application, commercial activity, or other external dissemination;
- commercial use of any kind.

3. Citation Requirement
Any authorized academic use must appropriately cite both:
(a) the associated scientific publication, when available; and
(b) the software repository and/or archived release.

The citation information provided in CITATION.cff should be used where applicable.

4. Authorship and Collaboration
Permission to use the Materials does not by itself create a right to authorship, and
authorship is not automatically required solely because the Materials are used.

However, if the copyright holder or contributors make substantial additional intellectual,
methodological, analytical, interpretive, software, or writing contributions to a subsequent
study, authorship should be discussed in good faith and determined according to the
authorship criteria of the target journal and applicable research-integrity standards.

Researchers wishing to adapt this framework to new datasets or research questions are
encouraged to contact the corresponding author to discuss permission and potential
collaboration.

